    "created_at": "2020-05-12T21:04:47Z",
    "updated_at": "2020-05-12T21:04:47Z",
    "body": "> 7.8.12 Aborting a Document doesn't say anything about whether or not to fire the load event to the Document (if it hasn't yet been fired).\r\n\r\nGenerally, when a specification doesn't say to do something, that means it's best not to do it :). So I'm not sure if there's much to do here on the spec side. It'll be good to write web platform tests disallowing such behavior, though!\r\n\r\n> It appears that all implementations do change the state, but only gecko is firing readystatechange.\r\n\r\nThat's frustrating; it seems like an important invariant that changing readyState emits readystatechange. Do you have a web platform test illustrating this? I'd be inclined to try to fix this in Chromium at least.",
