    "created_at": "2020-05-18T03:00:59Z",
    "updated_at": "2020-05-18T03:00:59Z",
    "body": "> That's frustrating; it seems like an important invariant that changing readyState emits readystatechange. Do you have a web platform test illustrating this? I'd be inclined to try to fix this in Chromium at least.\r\n\r\nI experimented with my testcase more, and it seems that readystatechange is only skipped in rare conditions.\r\n\r\nhttps://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D73994 has a tentative WPT that tries cancelling loads in two different ways, and only the former doesn't have a readystatechange event.\r\n",
